{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact H head 76b47a53086afefce115d3c609d849b4ee7b07ad on builder/typed-package-stories-h-20261110, tree e5a38d5c, all 34 artifacts, for request d49269fd under promise d43e33e1 and review request 909cdd3b. Define now builds a package manifest, its projections, its views and its roles from the definition value. A story runs on the maintained judges and writes scenario v1. The Lending and Counter manifests, the Lending scenario file and both pins keep their bytes.\n\nWhat I checked in the source:\n\n- Stories. `tell` in `packages/define/src/story.ts` validates the definition, then writes state only through `judgeGenesis`, `judgeAct` and `judgeTimed` drafts that `entryOf` seals and `applyEntry` folds. Each act reads its expected revisions from the fold through `alsoItems`. Each step compares the judged answer and every entry's input, effects and sends with the author's assertion, and `drainDue` writes timed firings inside the step that made them due. An unnamed `refused` does not match a named refusal. The TEST secrets are explicit public seeds, and `tell` zeroes them in `finally`.\n- Manifests. `manifest` derives entry, definitions, host profile, capabilities and the scope-reference connections. It refuses an act whose grant no role holds, both in its type and at run time. `projection` takes field types and nullability from the slots, sorts states and acts, bounds limits at 100, and refuses detached text.\n- Views. `checkViews` closes each view's shape, binds every template, fact and actor to the source's fields, and requires each control's act to sit on the source's item with the grant that a role holds. Row conditions go through E's `expression` serializer, which now has a row context that accepts only a projected field.\n- Provenance. `extend` checks the parent's digest and keeps the parent in a WeakMap. `compile` refuses a child that changes the parent's format, profile, genesis, capabilities, level, capacity or any inherited item, act, handler, timed rule or rule, and it reports the added names beside the unchanged `definition` and `digest`. `normalize` carries the mark across F's copy.\n- Act helpers. `open`, `transition` and `comment` gain a grant type parameter after the existing ones, with the same runtime data.\n- The boundary. Against main 74c958d0, the head changes nothing under the kernel packages, and the two new export paths `./package` and `./story` belong to `@generalbusiness/dap-define` only. The retained `dap.application.json` files, `examples/lending/scenarios/application.json`, `apps/counter/commitments-pin.ts` and `examples/lending/pin.ts` do not change.\n\nMy probes, on my own extracted copy of the head with its own workspace links and no shared validation slot:\n\n- `package.test.ts`, `story.test.ts` and `provenance.test.ts` pass 13 of 13.\n- `tsc -p tsconfig.json` and `tsc -p tsconfig.test.json` in `packages/define` exit 0, so the compile-only refusals in `package.types.ts`, `story.types.ts` and `expression.types.ts` hold.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- Scope. Main 74c958d0 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 34 paths that its 34 artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes with 16 checked and 0 flagged, `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean.\n- The follow-up. From gate checkpoint 9ff09d54, tree 6e6c51f0, the head changes only the note and the evidence manifest.\n- The gate. All 45 files of the evidence manifest match their recorded SHA-256 values, and `SHA256SUMS` verifies 44 of 44. `final-gate-summary.json` records head 9ff09d54, tree 6e6c51f0, an unchanged source, END cd268256, and actual exits of 0 for the gate, both drivers, the launcher, the external command and the analysis. It counts 5,869 passed cases and 3 planned skips.\n- The controls. I assess them as the note separates them. The first controller unit stays FAILED, exit 2, END bdf61b52. Within it, the Story mutant ran once and failed only the named unasserted-send case, so `story.test.ts` tells the mutant from the source. Ruling 21579e5e keeps that observation. The projection continuation, END 85e55551, ran the package owner once: the named missing-field case failed with child exit 1, and every custody exit reads 0. Both tests catch the mutant they guard against.\n- The browser. GitHub reports Page run 43031099285 and Card run 43031099363 as attempt 1, completed and successful, at exactly 76b47a53.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Package metadata now comes from one source, the definition value, so the editor rejects a view or grant that the manifest check refused only at run time before. The story builder adds no judge of its own. It drives the maintained judges and fold, so a scenario cannot assert an outcome the runtime would not produce. The kernel and every pinned byte stay unchanged, and P5 keeps parameters and derivation reserved with no second mechanism.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The change is authoring code. No runtime path imports Define, and the manifest grants no authority. TEST grants are stand-ins that the story writes with public seeds, and the story never contacts a service or a destination.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes for a later head:\n\n- The story's TEST grants carry `fresh: null`, as the CLI's local runner does (`packages/cli/src/application-local.ts:52`). A definition that sets `observing` makes `judgeAct` answer `authority-unavailable`, and `tell` stops with \"the story's act was not judged\". Lending and Counter do not observe. A later head can say that stories do not cover observing definitions.\n- `definitionProvenance` does not compare `name`, so an extension can rename itself. That fits an additive child, but `under` compares names, so the note could say so.\n\nThe note's history table keeps each failed or historical unit at its own head, and the CLI3 pass stays at 5f749419 without relabeling. This approval authorizes no 